Firmware host tests
===================

`test_native_protocol/test_main.cpp` contains Unity tests for the pure C++
parts of BLE dataset protocol v3:

- the IEEE CRC-32 known vector and incremental calculation;
- fragmented newline-delimited command assembly and overflow rejection;
- command, label, filename, uint32, uppercase-CRC, and sidecar-metadata parsing;
- the recording and file-operation state-machine primitives.

Run the Unity host suite with:

    pio test -e native_protocol_tests

On Windows the native environment needs the MSYS2 UCRT64 GCC directory at
`C:\msys64\ucrt64\bin` first in `PATH`.

These host tests do not exercise Arduino, Bluefruit, the physical BLE link,
QSPI/FAT operations, IMU sampling, or power-loss behavior. See
`../docs/testing_without_hardware.md` for all software gates and the later hardware
acceptance matrix.
